WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:00.893
- So Elisabeth Moss, as you saw,

00:00:00.893 --> 00:00:04.525
we know she beat you.
Like every time, right?

00:00:04.525 --> 00:00:06.360
- I don't know about every time.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:08.823
I think what she said
was she beat me once.

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:12.360
And then I refused to play again.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:14.460
But yeah, it was the championship.

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:15.540
She won the championship

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:16.830
and then the championship was over.

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:19.620
And then, you know, there was
never another championship.

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:20.700
What a shame.

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:22.380
- That is so sad.

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:24.420
No. What was the game of choice again?

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:25.920
- Well, she played Speed.

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:27.150
But we played a lot of games.

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:29.305
At the Madman base camp
there was dominoes,

00:00:29.305 --> 00:00:31.410
there was a lot of cards.

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:32.580
There was Heads Up! There was-

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:33.462
- Did you play X-Men dominoes?

00:00:33.462 --> 00:00:34.295
I love that.

00:00:34.295 --> 00:00:35.128
- We didn't play that there,

00:00:35.128 --> 00:00:36.640
but we played regular old dominoes.

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:39.310
There were a lot of games because

00:00:39.310 --> 00:00:40.970
we spent a lot of time there.

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:41.803
- Yeah.

00:00:41.803 --> 00:00:42.636
- Yeah.

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:45.780
- I was always there

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:47.010
because I'm in every scene.

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:47.843
- Yeah.

00:00:47.843 --> 00:00:51.240
- So I would sort of
run the game quotient.

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:52.530
And then if there was one

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:53.850
that I wasn't particularly good at

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:55.881
we shuffled that one
into the back of the...

00:00:55.881 --> 00:00:58.140
Into the back of the line.

00:00:58.140 --> 00:00:58.973
- We see who you are.

00:00:58.973 --> 00:00:59.806
- Yes.

00:00:59.806 --> 00:01:01.950
- So wait, you also love poker, right?

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:02.790
Do you do poker nights?

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:03.722
- I play poker.

00:01:03.722 --> 00:01:04.555
- Okay.

00:01:04.555 --> 00:01:05.850
- I've been in a

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:07.080
actually a game

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:08.911
of poker that's been
running every week since

00:01:08.911 --> 00:01:11.940
before I started Mad
Men, which would've been-

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:12.773
- What?

00:01:12.773 --> 00:01:13.680
Back in the early 2000s.

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:16.260
But I love playing poker. It's fun.

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:18.486
It's more fun to just
get your friends together

00:01:18.486 --> 00:01:20.310
and sit around a table and talk.

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:21.143
- 100%. And it's just kind of the vessel

00:01:21.143 --> 00:01:21.976
for that whole gambling scenario.

00:01:21.976 --> 00:01:23.700
- Absolutely.

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:24.600
- Okay. I love it.

